From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ps4-gladius <ps4-gladius@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] start: set the module's environment as well as the title's.

The PS4 SDK ships libc only as a static archive, so the title and every PRX
carry a private __environ. pw_wine_start_environment sets WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR
through ops->set_env, which writes the title's copy; Wine runs inside ntdll and
reads its own, which is empty:

    WINE wine: cannot get path to ntdll.so (set WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR)

with the title still reporting environment status=0.

Linking the shared libc unifies the two, but drags malloc, exit and the whole
__cxa_* family onto libc.prx -- 88 symbols -- and the title then dies with
PRX_NOT_RESOLVED_FUNCTION. Instead the module exports pw_ps4_setenv
(src/native/pw_prx_env_ps4.c in the port), which writes its own environ, and
the same values go to both. Where the export is absent, as on PS5, nothing
changes.
---
diff --git a/src/pw_wine_start.c b/src/pw_wine_start.c
index 84b4b71..80ab1e4 100644
--- a/src/pw_wine_start.c
+++ b/src/pw_wine_start.c
@@ -76,6 +76,25 @@ int pw_wine_start_environment(PwWineStart *start, const PwWineStartConfig *confi
         (config->extra_env_count && !config->extra_env))
         return PW_ERR_PRECONDITION;
     /* WINELOADERNOEXEC keeps __wine_main from re-executing a loader. */
+    /* ⚠ PS4: the title and each PRX have a private environ, because the SDK
+     * ships libc only as a static archive. ops->set_env writes the title's,
+     * which Wine -- running inside ntdll -- never sees. pw_ps4_setenv is
+     * exported by the module and writes its own, so set both. */
+    {
+        int (*module_setenv)(const char *, const char *) =
+            (int (*)(const char *, const char *))
+            (uintptr_t)pw_prx_lookup(start->descriptor, "pw_ps4_setenv");
+        if (module_setenv) {
+            module_setenv("WINEPREFIX", config->prefix);
+            module_setenv("WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR", config->ntdll_dir);
+            module_setenv("WINELOADERNOEXEC", "1");
+            for (uint32_t i = 0; i < config->extra_env_count; i++) {
+                const PwWineStartEnv *env = &config->extra_env[i];
+                if (env->name && env->value) module_setenv(env->name, env->value);
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     if ((status = ops->set_env("WINEPREFIX", config->prefix)) != 0 ||
         (status = ops->set_env("WINE_PS5_NTDLL_DIR", config->ntdll_dir)) != 0 ||
         (status = ops->set_env("WINELOADERNOEXEC", "1")) != 0)
